# Feature Specification: Zigzag Patterns Engine

Feature Branch: `009-zigzag-patterns-engine`
Created: 2026-10-28
Status: Draft
Input: User description: "A library that detects Zigzag patterns (Ideal 5-3-5, Simple 3-3-3, Anti 3-5-5), validates the C > 100% B rule, classifies by wave C size (truncated/normal/extended), predicts post-pattern move (38.2%, 61.8%), and detects AB=CD subset."

## User Scenarios & Testing

### User Story 1 - Detect Zigzag Structure (Priority: P1)

The engine detects Zigzag structure (5-3-5, 3-3-3, 3-5-5) and validates the C > 100% B rule.

**Independent Test:** Given A=5, B=3, C=5 with C > 100% B, the engine returns `pattern="Zigzag Ideal"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given A=5, B=3, C=5 with C > 100% B, When detecting, Then returns `type="Ideal"`.
- Given A=3, B=3, C=3 with C > 100% B and B < 61.8% A, When detecting, Then returns `type="Simple"`.
- Given A=3, B=5, C=5 with C > 100% B, When detecting, Then returns `type="Anti"`.
- Given C < 100% B, When detecting, Then returns `error="Zigzag requires C ≥ 100% B"`.

### User Story 2 - Classify by Wave C Size (Priority: P1)

The engine classifies Zigzag as Truncated (61.8-100%), Normal (100-161.8%), or Extended (>161.8%) based on Fibonacci projection.

**Independent Test:** Given C = 120% A, the engine returns `class="Normal"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given C = 80% A, When classifying, Then returns `class="Truncated"`.
- Given C = 120% A, When classifying, Then returns `class="Normal"`.
- Given C = 180% A, When classifying, Then returns `class="Extended"`.
- Given C = 50% A, When classifying, Then returns `error="C < 61.8% is invalid"`.

### User Story 3 - Predict Post-Pattern Move (Priority: P1)

The engine predicts post-pattern move based on Zigzag type and wave B size.

**Independent Test:** Given Normal Zigzag with B > 61.8%, the engine returns `target="61.8% of whole pattern"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given Normal Zigzag + B > 61.8% A, When predicting, Then returns `target=0.618` (whole pattern).
- Given Normal Zigzag + B < 61.8% A, When predicting, Then returns `target=0.382` (whole pattern).
- Given Extended Zigzag + B < 61.8% A, When predicting, Then returns `target=0.236` (whole pattern).
- Given Truncated Zigzag + B > 61.8% A, When predicting, Then returns `target=0.618 or 0.81` (of wave C).

### User Story 4 - Detect AB=CD Subset (Priority: P2)

The engine detects AB=CD subset (wave A length ≈ wave C length) within Zigzag Ideal.

**Independent Test:** Given A=100, C=100, the engine returns `ab_cd=True`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given A=100, C=100, When detecting, Then returns `ab_cd=True, tolerance=0`.
- Given A=100, C=105, When detecting, Then returns `ab_cd=True, tolerance=5%`.
- Given A=100, C=150, When detecting, Then returns `ab_cd=False`.

### User Story 5 - Validate Zigzag at Market End (Priority: P2)

The engine flags Zigzag at market end as lower confidence (more alternative patterns possible).

**Independent Test:** Given Zigzag at market end with no confirmation, the engine returns `confidence=0.5`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given Zigzag in past data, When validating, Then returns `confidence=0.85`.
- Given Zigzag at market end + confirmation (volume, support), When validating, Then returns `confidence=0.7`.
- Given Zigzag at market end without confirmation, When validating, Then returns `confidence=0.5`.

### Edge Cases

- **A=3, B=3, C=3 with B > 61.8% A:** Not pure Simple Zigzag; flag as "Complex".
- **A=5, B=5, C=3:** Invalid structure (error).
- **C = 100% B exactly:** Boundary case (valid).
- **C = 60% A:** Invalid (below truncated minimum).
- **A=100, C=99.5:** Not AB=CD (tolerance < 0.5%).
- **AB=CD with A=100, C=101:** AB=CD with 1% tolerance.
- **Zigzag in wave 2 with B > 100%:** Anti-cycle (not zigzag).
- **Zigzag in wave 4 with C > 100% B:** Valid.
- **Zigzag at market end with terminal nearby:** Alternative pattern warning.

## Requirements

### Functional Requirements

- **FR-001:** System MUST detect Zigzag structure (5-3-5, 3-3-3, 3-5-5).
- **FR-002:** System MUST validate C > 100% B rule (strict).
- **FR-003:** System MUST classify by wave C size (Truncated/Normal/Extended).
- **FR-004:** System MUST predict post-pattern move (38.2%, 61.8%, 23.6%, 81%).
- **FR-005:** System MUST detect AB=CD subset within Ideal Zigzag.
- **FR-006:** System MUST flag Zigzag at market end as lower confidence.
- **FR-007:** System MUST distinguish Simple Zigzag (B < 61.8%) from Complex (B > 61.8%).
- **FR-008:** System MUST expose all functionality via CLI (JSON in/out).

### Key Entities

- **ZigzagInput:** `{wave_a, wave_b, wave_c, wave_b_max_pct: float}`
- **ZigzagResult:** `{type, class, post_pattern_target, ab_cd, confidence, warnings}`
- **WaveStructure:** `{label, sub_wave_count, length}`

## Success Criteria

- **SC-001:** Zigzag structure detection accuracy ≥ 95%.
- **SC-002:** C > 100% B validation = 100% (strict).
- **SC-003:** Classification (Truncated/Normal/Extended) accuracy ≥ 95%.
- **SC-004:** Post-pattern move prediction accuracy ≥ 85%.
- **SC-005:** AB=CD detection precision ≥ 90%.
- **SC-006:** Market-end confidence adjustment accuracy ≥ 90%.
- **SC-007:** CLI responds in < 100ms for 10 zigzags.
