# Feature Specification: Flat Pattern Types Engine

Feature Branch: `012-flat-pattern-types-engine`
Created: 2026-10-28
Status: Draft
Input: User description: "A library that classifies Flat into 8 types with precise ratios, validates 3-3-5 structure for all types, enforces B > 61.8% rule, determines when to use Flat (past only, not market end), and provides flat-as-knot-untangler recommendations for complex counts."

## User Scenarios & Testing

### User Story 1 - Classify 8 Flat Types (Priority: P1)

The engine classifies Flat into 8 types based on precise B/A and C/B ratios.

**Independent Test:** Given B=90%, C=90%, the engine returns `type="Regular"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given B=90%, C=90%, When classifying, Then returns `Regular`.
- Given B=70%, C=90%, When classifying, Then returns `B-Deficient`.
- Given B=90%, C=70%, When classifying, Then returns `C-Deficient`.
- Given B=70%, C=70%, When classifying, Then returns `Double-Deficient`.
- Given B=110%, C=105%, When classifying, Then returns `Irregular`.
- Given B=110%, C=70%, When classifying, Then returns `Irregular-Deficient`.
- Given B=150%, C=120%, When classifying, Then returns `Irregular-Extended`.
- Given B=110%, C=50%, When classifying, Then returns `Running (deprecated)`.

### User Story 2 - Validate 3-3-5 Structure (Priority: P1)

All 8 Flat types MUST have 3-3-5 structure.

**Independent Test:** Given A=3, B=3, C=5, the engine returns `valid_structure=True`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given A=3, B=3, C=5, When validating, Then returns `valid_structure=True`.
- Given A=5, B=3, C=5, When validating, Then returns `valid_structure=False` (Zigzag).
- Given A=3, B=3, C=3, When validating, Then returns `valid_structure=False` (Simple Zigzag).

### User Story 3 - Enforce B > 61.8% Rule (Priority: P1)

All Flat types MUST have B > 61.8% of A.

**Independent Test:** Given B=70% A, the engine returns `b_valid=True`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given B=70% A, When validating, Then returns `b_valid=True`.
- Given B=61% A, When validating, Then returns `b_valid=False` (Simple Zigzag).
- Given B=61.8% A, When validating, Then returns `b_valid=True` (boundary).

### User Story 4 - Restrict Flat at Market End (Priority: P1)

The engine flags Flat at market end as "not recommended" (more alternatives possible).

**Independent Test:** Given Flat at market end without confirmation, the engine returns `usable=False`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given Flat in past data, When evaluating, Then returns `usable=True, confidence=0.8`.
- Given Flat at market end + confirmation, When evaluating, Then returns `usable=True, confidence=0.5`.
- Given Flat at market end without confirmation, When evaluating, Then returns `usable=False, reason="Too many alternatives at market end"`.

### User Story 5 - Recommend Flat as Knot-Untangler (Priority: P2)

The engine recommends Flat when standard patterns (Zigzag, Triangle) fail to untangle a count.

**Independent Test:** Given a count where wave 4 has 5+ sub-waves, the engine recommends `flat_as_knot_untangler=True`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given wave 4 = 3 sub-waves, When recommending, Then returns `flat_as_knot_untangler=False` (standard count).
- Given wave 4 = 5+ sub-waves + count fails, When recommending, Then returns `flat_as_knot_untangler=True`.
- Given wave 4 = 5+ sub-waves + no count fails, When recommending, Then returns `flat_as_knot_untangler=False, reason="Review count first"`.

### Edge Cases

- **B = 61.8% A exactly:** Boundary; still valid Flat.
- **B = 100% A:** Boundary Regular/Irregular.
- **B = 138.2% A:** Boundary Irregular/Irregular-Extended.
- **C = 61.8% B exactly:** Boundary for C-Deficient.
- **C = 81% B:** Boundary C-Deficient/C-Regular.
- **Running Flat (B > 100%, C < 61.8%):** Deprecated in course; flag as "not recommended".
- **Double-Deficient + market end:** Very low confidence (0.3).
- **Flat with C = Diagonal:** Valid; flag C sub-structure.
- **Flat with C = Terminal:** Valid; flag C sub-structure.
- **Wave 4 = 5 sub-waves, Zigzag possible:** Prefer Zigzag over Flat.
- **Wave 4 = 5 sub-waves, Zigzag impossible:** Use Flat.
- **Wave 4 = 5 sub-waves, Flat impossible:** Use Complex (combination).

## Requirements

### Functional Requirements

- **FR-001:** System MUST classify Flat into 8 types.
- **FR-002:** System MUST validate 3-3-5 structure for all Flat types.
- **FR-003:** System MUST enforce B > 61.8% rule.
- **FR-004:** System MUST restrict Flat at market end (unless confirmed).
- **FR-005:** System MUST recommend Flat as knot-untangler when standard patterns fail.
- **FR-006:** System MUST flag Running Flat as deprecated.
- **FR-007:** System MUST compute confidence per Flat type.
- **FR-008:** System MUST detect C sub-structure (Ideal/Diagonal/Terminal).
- **FR-009:** System MUST expose all functionality via CLI (JSON in/out).

### Key Entities

- **FlatRequest:** `{wave_a, wave_b, wave_c, is_market_end, has_confirmation, c_sub_structure, context}`
- **FlatResponse:** `{type, b_pct_a, c_pct_b, valid_structure, b_valid, usable, confidence, c_sub_structure, knot_untangler, warnings}`
- **FlatType:** Enum (8 types)

## Success Criteria

- **SC-001:** 8-type classification accuracy ≥ 95%.
- **SC-002:** 3-3-5 structure validation = 100% (strict).
- **SC-003:** B > 61.8% rule = 100% (strict).
- **SC-004:** Market-end restriction = 100% (strict).
- **SC-005:** Knot-untangler recommendation accuracy ≥ 85%.
- **SC-006:** CLI responds in < 100ms for 10 flats.
