# Feature Specification: Complex Patterns Advanced Engine

Feature Branch: `016-complex-patterns-advanced-engine`
Created: 2026-10-28
Status: Draft
Input: User description: "A library that detects all 9 standard complex combinations (Z-X-Z, Z-X-F, Z-X-T, F-X-Z, F-X-F, F-X-T, T-X-Z, T-X-F, T-X-T) plus main-pattern combinations (I-X-Z, G-X-F, T-X-T, etc.), validates X-Wave type (single, zigzag, impulsive), and recommends simplest counting approach."

## User Scenarios & Testing

### User Story 1 - Detect 9 Standard Combinations (Priority: P1)

The engine detects all 9 standard complex combinations.

**Independent Test:** Given Zigzag + X + Zigzag, the engine returns `pattern="Z-X-Z"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given Z + X + Z, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="Z-X-Z"`.
- Given Z + X + F, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="Z-X-F"`.
- Given Z + X + T, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="Z-X-T"`.
- Given F + X + Z, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="F-X-Z"`.
- Given F + X + F, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="F-X-F"`.
- Given F + X + T, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="F-X-T"`.
- Given T + X + Z, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="T-X-Z"`.
- Given T + X + F, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="T-X-F"`.
- Given T + X + T, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="T-X-T"`.

### User Story 2 - Detect Main-Pattern Combinations (Priority: P1)

The engine detects combinations with main patterns (I, G, T-term).

**Independent Test:** Given Ideal + X + Zigzag, the engine returns `pattern="I-X-Z"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given I + X + Z, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="I-X-Z"`.
- Given G + X + F, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="G-X-F"`.
- Given T-term + X + T-tri, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="T-X-T"`.
- Given I + X + I, When detecting, Then returns `pattern="I-X-I"` (very rare).

### User Story 3 - Validate X-Wave Type (Priority: P1)

The engine validates X-Wave type: single wave (≥3 candles), Zigzag (5-3-5, 3-3-3, 3-5-5), or impulsive (no structure).

**Independent Test:** Given X-Wave = 3 candles, the engine returns `x_valid=True, x_type="single"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given X-Wave = 3 candles, When validating, Then returns `x_type="single"`.
- Given X-Wave = Zigzag (5-3-5), When validating, Then returns `x_type="zigzag_ideal"`.
- Given X-Wave = impulsive (no structure), When validating, Then returns `x_type="impulsive"`.
- Given X-Wave = 2 candles, When validating, Then returns `x_valid=False`.

### User Story 4 - Recommend Simplest Counting (Priority: P1)

The engine recommends simplest counting (prefer Z over Z-X-Z, prefer Z-X-Z over Z-X-Z-X-Z).

**Independent Test:** Given Z possible + Z-X-Z possible, the engine returns `recommend="simple"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given Z possible, When recommending, Then returns `recommend="simple"`.
- Given Z impossible + Z-X-Z possible, When recommending, Then returns `recommend="complex_2"` (2 patterns).
- Given Z-X-Z impossible + Z-X-Z-X-Z possible, When recommending, Then returns `recommend="complex_3"` (3 patterns).

### User Story 5 - Detect Non-Standard Combinations (Priority: P2)

The engine detects non-standard combinations (Z-X-F-X-Z, Z-X-Z-X-Z, etc.).

**Independent Test:** Given Z + X + F + X + Z, the engine returns `standard=False, pattern="Z-X-F-X-Z"`.

**Acceptance Scenarios:**
- Given Z-X-Z (2 patterns), When detecting, Then returns `standard=True`.
- Given Z-X-Z-X-Z (3 patterns), When detecting, Then returns `standard=False`.
- Given Z-X-F-X-Z (3 patterns), When detecting, Then returns `standard=False, complexity="high"`.

### Edge Cases

- **X-Wave = 2 candles:** Invalid.
- **X-Wave = 3 candles + strong trend:** Valid (single).
- **Z-X-Z with wave 2 > 100% wave 1:** Invalid (violates rule 1).
- **Z-X-F-X-Z with no X-Wave structure:** Invalid.
- **T-X-T (both Triangle):** Valid (rare).
- **I-X-I (both Ideal):** Valid (very rare).
- **G-X-G (both Diagonal):** Valid (rare).
- **Combination with >4 patterns:** Flag as "too complex; recount".
- **Complex at market end without confirmation:** Low confidence.
- **Simple possible + complex possible + same target:** Prefer simple.
- **Simple possible + complex possible + different targets:** Use simple as primary, complex as secondary.
- **Z-X-Z with X-Wave = Zigzag:** Valid and common.

## Requirements

### Functional Requirements

- **FR-001:** System MUST detect all 9 standard combinations.
- **FR-002:** System MUST detect main-pattern combinations (I-X-Z, G-X-F, etc.).
- **FR-003:** System MUST validate X-Wave type (single, zigzag, impulsive).
- **FR-004:** System MUST recommend simplest counting approach.
- **FR-005:** System MUST detect non-standard combinations (3+ patterns).
- **FR-006:** System MUST enforce 3 cardinal rules.
- **FR-007:** System MUST reduce confidence for complex/non-standard.
- **FR-008:** System MUST flag >4 patterns as "too complex".
- **FR-009:** System MUST expose all functionality via CLI (JSON in/out).

### Key Entities

- **Pattern:** `{abbreviation, waves}`
- **ComplexRequest:** `{components: [Pattern], x_waves: [Pattern], is_market_end}`
- **ComplexResponse:** `{pattern, standard, x_types, recommend, complexity, confidence, warnings}`
- **Recommendation:** Enum: `SIMPLE, COMPLEX_2, COMPLEX_3, RECOUNT`

## Success Criteria

- **SC-001:** 9 standard combination detection accuracy ≥ 95%.
- **SC-002:** Main-pattern combination detection accuracy ≥ 90%.
- **SC-003:** X-Wave type validation = 100%.
- **SC-004:** Simplest counting recommendation accuracy ≥ 95%.
- **SC-005:** Non-standard detection accuracy ≥ 90%.
- **SC-006:** CLI responds in < 100ms for 10 complexes.
